{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 47, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e4b-it", "content": "## Lost (and Found) in Japan\n\nJust back from an incredible trip to Japan, and I'm already dreaming of going back! It was a whirlwind of ancient traditions and futuristic technology, a truly captivating contrast.\n\nMy journey started in Tokyo, a city that assaults the senses in the best way possible. Neon lights, bustling crowds, and the aroma of street food everywhere! I spent hours exploring Shibuya Crossing, marveling at the organized chaos.  A visit to the serene Meiji Jingu Shrine provided a much-needed moment of peace amidst the urban sprawl.\n\nFrom Tokyo, I took the Shinkansen (bullet train) to Kyoto.  The speed and efficiency were astounding! Kyoto felt like stepping back in time.  I wandered through stunning temples like Kinkaku-ji (the Golden Pavilion) and Kiyomizu-dera, and got wonderfully lost in the Gion district, hoping to catch a glimpse of a geisha.\n\nThe food was, of course, phenomenal.  From delicate sushi and ramen to savory okonomiyaki, every meal was a delight. I even tried (and enjoyed!) takoyaki – octopus balls!\n\nBeyond the major cities, I explored some smaller towns, soaking up the local culture. The politeness and respect of the Japanese people were truly remarkable. \n\nJapan is a country that stays with you long after you've left. It's a place of beauty, history, and innovation – a must-visit for any traveler!\n\n\n\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "##", "logprob": -1.6689286894688848e-06}, {"token": "▁Lost", "logprob": -0.0011177966371178627}, {"token": "▁(", "logprob": -0.18502815067768097}, {"token": "and", "logprob": -8.344646857949556e-07}, {"token": "▁Found", "logprob": -0.0015026956098154187}, {"token": ")", "logprob": -0.1426810771226883}, {"token": "▁in", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "▁Japan", "logprob": -0.11408442258834839}, {"token": "\n\n", "logprob": -0.25964632630348206}, {"token": "Just", "logprob": -0.791698276996